#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Diagnose why L1 ProMatch predecoding (PU) disagrees with flat PyMatching (U0).

Two subcommands:

  replay  Replay the regression/recovery samples retained in a paired collection's
          ``summary.json`` bit-exactly, then classify every committed prematch
          against the flat MWPM solution ``M*`` for the same shot: does M* match
          the same pair, and if not, where did M* send each endpoint (yoke hub,
          true boundary, next window, terminal layer, in-domain)?  Also reports
          how the residual matching re-routed yoke/boundary edges, i.e. how a
          local commit turned into a two-observable logical error.

  probe   Sample fresh shots for a cell (from a protocol or explicit d/n/r/p),
          run PU and U0, and report activation, commits per stage, the
          per-stage rate at which commits disagree with M*, the M*-partner
          kinds of disagreeing endpoints, and paired U0/PU failures.

Both are diagnostics only: they are not claim-bearing and never write into a
collection directory.  Single process; one native thread.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

